(Chapter 1: Five Main Articulation Zones \(Al-Makharij Al-Ammah\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 731.8899999999999864 Td
(1. Al-Jawf \(The Empty Space of Throat and Mouth\): Produces the three Madd letters — Alif \(always) Tj
T* (preceded by Fathah\), Waw Sakinah \(preceded by Dammah\), and Ya Sakinah \(preceded by Kasrah\).) Tj
T* (Each natural Madd \(Madd Asli\) is held smoothly for two harakat \(two counts\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 666.8899999999999864 Td
(2. Al-Halq \(The Throat\): Houses six throat letters divided into three levels. Deep throat \(Aqsa) Tj
T* (al-Halq\) produces Hamzah and Ha. Middle throat \(Wasat al-Halq\) produces Ayn and Ha. Upper) Tj
T* (throat \(Adna al-Halq\) produces Ghayn and Kha.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 601.8899999999999864 Td
(3. Al-Lisan \(The Tongue\): Contains ten sub-points producing eighteen Arabic letters including Qaf,) Tj
T* (Kaf, Jeem, Sheen, Ya, Dad, Lam, Noon, Ra, and the dental letters.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 553.8899999999999864 Td
(4. Ash-Shafatan \(The Two Lips\): Produces Fa, Ba, Meem, and consonant Waw.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 522.8899999999999864 Td
(5. Al-Khayshum \(The Nasal Passage\): Source of Ghunnah \(nasalization held for two counts in Noon) Tj
T* (and Meem Mushaddadah, Idgham, Ikhfa, and Iqlab\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
