(Chapter 2: Rules of Nun Sakinah and Tanween) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 731.8899999999999864 Td
(Izhar Halqi \(Clear Pronunciation\): Applied before the six throat letters. No extra nasalization beyond) Tj
T* (the natural consonant sound.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 683.8899999999999864 Td
(Idgham \(Merging\): Merging Noon Sakinah or Tanween into the six letters gathered in the mnemonic) Tj
T* (YARMALUN. Complete merging without Ghunnah occurs before Lam and Ra; merging with) Tj
T* (Ghunnah occurs before Ya, Noon, Meem, and Waw.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 618.8899999999999864 Td
(Iqlab \(Conversion\): When Noon Sakinah or Tanween is followed by Ba, the sound transforms into a) Tj
T* (concealed Meem with two counts of Ghunnah.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 570.8899999999999864 Td
(Ikhfa Haqiqi \(Concealment\): Applied smoothly with light nasalization before the remaining fifteen) Tj
T* (Arabic letters.) Tj
ET
